# Cloudflare Pages rewrites. The payment link the bot sends is /pay/<token>, which is a
# path rather than a query string on purpose: it is what a customer sees in their address
# bar, and ?t=... reads like something that can be edited.
#
# 200 rather than 301: the browser must keep the /pay/<token> URL so the page can read the
# token back out of it. A redirect would throw the token away before the JavaScript runs.
/pay/*  /pay.html  200

